window.NEVSKY_VERSES={"01-01":["In the beginning was the Word, and the Word was with God, and the Word was God.","John 1:1"],"01-02":["And the light shineth in darkness; and the darkness comprehended it not.","John 1:5"],"01-03":["And the Word was made flesh, and dwelt among us, (and we beheld his glory, the glory as of the only begotten of the Father,) full of grace and truth.","John 1:14"],"01-04":["And lo a voice from heaven, saying, This is my beloved Son, in whom I am well pleased.","Matthew 3:17"],"01-05":["For unto us a child is born, unto us a son is given: and the government shall be upon his shoulder: and his name shall be called Wonderful, Counsellor, The mighty God, The everlasting Father, The Prince of Peace.","Isaiah 9:6"],"01-06":["Glory to God in the highest, and on earth peace, good will toward men.","Luke 2:14"],"01-07":["Blessed are the poor in spirit: for theirs is the kingdom of heaven.","Matthew 5:3"],"01-08":["Blessed are they that mourn: for they shall be comforted.","Matthew 5:4"],"01-09":["Blessed are the meek: for they shall inherit the earth.","Matthew 5:5"],"01-10":["Blessed are they which do hunger and thirst after righteousness: for they shall be filled.","Matthew 5:6"],"01-11":["Blessed are the merciful: for they shall obtain mercy.","Matthew 5:7"],"01-12":["Blessed are the pure in heart: for they shall see God.","Matthew 5:8"],"01-13":["Blessed are the peacemakers: for they shall be called the children of God.","Matthew 5:9"],"01-14":["Ye are the light of the world. A city that is set on an hill cannot be hid.","Matthew 5:14"],"01-15":["Let your light so shine before men, that they may see your good works, and glorify your Father which is in heaven.","Matthew 5:16"],"01-16":["But I say unto you, Love your enemies, bless them that curse you, do good to them that hate you, and pray for them which despitefully use you, and persecute you…","Matthew 5:44"],"01-17":["But thou, when thou prayest, enter into thy closet, and when thou hast shut thy door, pray to thy Father which is in secret; and thy Father which seeth in secret shall reward thee openly.","Matthew 6:6"],"01-18":["For where your treasure is, there will your heart be also.","Matthew 6:21"],"01-19":["But seek ye first the kingdom of God, and his righteousness; and all these things shall be added unto you.","Matthew 6:33"],"01-20":["Take therefore no thought for the morrow: for the morrow shall take thought for the things of itself. Sufficient unto the day is the evil thereof.","Matthew 6:34"],"01-21":["Ask, and it shall be given you; seek, and ye shall find; knock, and it shall be opened unto you…","Matthew 7:7"],"01-22":["Therefore all things whatsoever ye would that men should do to you, do ye even so to them: for this is the law and the prophets.","Matthew 7:12"],"01-23":["Come unto me, all ye that labour and are heavy laden, and I will give you rest.","Matthew 11:28"],"01-24":["Take my yoke upon you, and learn of me; for I am meek and lowly in heart: and ye shall find rest unto your souls.","Matthew 11:29"],"01-25":["For where two or three are gathered together in my name, there am I in the midst of them.","Matthew 18:20"],"01-26":["Jesus said unto him, Thou shalt love the Lord thy God with all thy heart, and with all thy soul, and with all thy mind.","Matthew 22:37"],"01-27":["And the second is like unto it, Thou shalt love thy neighbour as thyself.","Matthew 22:39"],"01-28":["And the King shall answer and say unto them, Verily I say unto you, Inasmuch as ye have done it unto one of the least of these my brethren, ye have done it unto me.","Matthew 25:40"],"01-29":["Teaching them to observe all things whatsoever I have commanded you: and, lo, I am with you alway, even unto the end of the world. Amen.","Matthew 28:20"],"01-30":["And saying, The time is fulfilled, and the kingdom of God is at hand: repent ye, and believe the gospel.","Mark 1:15"],"01-31":["Jesus said unto him, If thou canst believe, all things are possible to him that believeth.","Mark 9:23"],"02-01":["And Jesus looking upon them saith, With men it is impossible, but not with God: for with God all things are possible.","Mark 10:27"],"02-02":["Therefore I say unto you, What things soever ye desire, when ye pray, believe that ye receive them, and ye shall have them.","Mark 11:24"],"02-03":["And thou shalt love the Lord thy God with all thy heart, and with all thy soul, and with all thy mind, and with all thy strength: this is the first commandment.","Mark 12:30"],"02-04":["For with God nothing shall be impossible.","Luke 1:37"],"02-05":["And Mary said, My soul doth magnify the Lord, And my spirit hath rejoiced in God my Saviour.","Luke 1:46-47"],"02-06":["Lord, now lettest thou thy servant depart in peace, according to thy word: For mine eyes have seen thy salvation…","Luke 2:29-30"],"02-07":["And as ye would that men should do to you, do ye also to them likewise.","Luke 6:31"],"02-08":["Be ye therefore merciful, as your Father also is merciful.","Luke 6:36"],"02-09":["Judge not, and ye shall not be judged: condemn not, and ye shall not be condemned: forgive, and ye shall be forgiven…","Luke 6:37"],"02-10":["But he said, Yea rather, blessed are they that hear the word of God, and keep it.","Luke 11:28"],"02-11":["For where your treasure is, there will your heart be also.","Luke 12:34"],"02-12":["I say unto you, that likewise joy shall be in heaven over one sinner that repenteth, more than over ninety and nine just persons, which need no repentance.","Luke 15:7"],"02-13":["And the publican, standing afar off, would not lift up so much as his eyes unto heaven, but smote upon his breast, saying, God be merciful to me a sinner.","Luke 18:13"],"02-14":["And he said, The things which are impossible with men are possible with God.","Luke 18:27"],"02-15":["Heaven and earth shall pass away: but my words shall not pass away.","Luke 21:33"],"02-16":["And he said unto Jesus, Lord, remember me when thou comest into thy kingdom.","Luke 23:42"],"02-17":["For God so loved the world, that he gave his only begotten Son, that whosoever believeth in him should not perish, but have everlasting life.","John 3:16"],"02-18":["For God sent not his Son into the world to condemn the world; but that the world through him might be saved.","John 3:17"],"02-19":["God is a Spirit: and they that worship him must worship him in spirit and in truth.","John 4:24"],"02-20":["And Jesus said unto them, I am the bread of life: he that cometh to me shall never hunger; and he that believeth on me shall never thirst.","John 6:35"],"02-21":["I am the living bread which came down from heaven: if any man eat of this bread, he shall live for ever: and the bread that I will give is my flesh, which I will give for the life of the world.","John 6:51"],"02-22":["Then spake Jesus again unto them, saying, I am the light of the world: he that followeth me shall not walk in darkness, but shall have the light of life.","John 8:12"],"02-23":["And ye shall know the truth, and the truth shall make you free.","John 8:32"],"02-24":["I am the good shepherd: the good shepherd giveth his life for the sheep.","John 10:11"],"02-25":["My sheep hear my voice, and I know them, and they follow me…","John 10:27"],"02-26":["Jesus said unto her, I am the resurrection, and the life: he that believeth in me, though he were dead, yet shall he live…","John 11:25"],"02-27":["A new commandment I give unto you, That ye love one another; as I have loved you, that ye also love one another.","John 13:34"],"02-28":["By this shall all men know that ye are my disciples, if ye have love one to another.","John 13:35"],"02-29":["Jesus saith unto him, I am the way, the truth, and the life: no man cometh unto the Father, but by me.","John 14:6"],"03-01":["Peace I leave with you, my peace I give unto you: not as the world giveth, give I unto you. Let not your heart be troubled, neither let it be afraid.","John 14:27"],"03-02":["I am the vine, ye are the branches: He that abideth in me, and I in him, the same bringeth forth much fruit: for without me ye can do nothing.","John 15:5"],"03-03":["As the Father hath loved me, so have I loved you: continue ye in my love.","John 15:9"],"03-04":["This is my commandment, That ye love one another, as I have loved you.","John 15:12"],"03-05":["Greater love hath no man than this, that a man lay down his life for his friends.","John 15:13"],"03-06":["These things I have spoken unto you, that in me ye might have peace. In the world ye shall have tribulation: but be of good cheer; I have overcome the world.","John 16:33"],"03-07":["And this is life eternal, that they might know thee the only true God, and Jesus Christ, whom thou hast sent.","John 17:3"],"03-08":["Jesus saith unto him, Thomas, because thou hast seen me, thou hast believed: blessed are they that have not seen, and yet have believed.","John 20:29"],"03-09":["And it shall come to pass, that whosoever shall call on the name of the Lord shall be saved.","Acts 2:21"],"03-10":["Neither is there salvation in any other: for there is none other name under heaven given among men, whereby we must be saved.","Acts 4:12"],"03-11":["And they said, Believe on the Lord Jesus Christ, and thou shalt be saved, and thy house.","Acts 16:31"],"03-12":["For in him we live, and move, and have our being; as certain also of your own poets have said, For we are also his offspring.","Acts 17:28"],"03-13":["I have shewed you all things, how that so labouring ye ought to support the weak, and to remember the words of the Lord Jesus, how he said, It is more blessed to give than to receive.","Acts 20:35"],"03-14":["And hope maketh not ashamed; because the love of God is shed abroad in our hearts by the Holy Ghost which is given unto us.","Romans 5:5"],"03-15":["But God commendeth his love toward us, in that, while we were yet sinners, Christ died for us.","Romans 5:8"],"03-16":["For the wages of sin is death; but the gift of God is eternal life through Jesus Christ our Lord.","Romans 6:23"],"03-17":["For I reckon that the sufferings of this present time are not worthy to be compared with the glory which shall be revealed in us.","Romans 8:18"],"03-18":["And we know that all things work together for good to them that love God, to them who are the called according to his purpose.","Romans 8:28"],"03-19":["What shall we then say to these things? If God be for us, who can be against us?","Romans 8:31"],"03-20":["For I am persuaded, that neither death, nor life, nor angels, nor principalities, nor powers, nor things present, nor things to come, Nor height, nor depth, nor any other creature, shall be able to separate us from the love of God, which is in Christ Jesus our Lord.","Romans 8:38-39"],"03-21":["That if thou shalt confess with thy mouth the Lord Jesus, and shalt believe in thine heart that God hath raised him from the dead, thou shalt be saved.","Romans 10:9"],"03-22":["And be not conformed to this world: but be ye transformed by the renewing of your mind, that ye may prove what is that good, and acceptable, and perfect, will of God.","Romans 12:2"],"03-23":["Rejoicing in hope; patient in tribulation; continuing instant in prayer…","Romans 12:12"],"03-24":["Rejoice with them that do rejoice, and weep with them that weep.","Romans 12:15"],"03-25":["Be not overcome of evil, but overcome evil with good.","Romans 12:21"],"03-26":["Love worketh no ill to his neighbour: therefore love is the fulfilling of the law.","Romans 13:10"],"03-27":["For whether we live, we live unto the Lord; and whether we die, we die unto the Lord: whether we live therefore, or die, we are the Lord’s.","Romans 14:8"],"03-28":["Now the God of hope fill you with all joy and peace in believing, that ye may abound in hope, through the power of the Holy Ghost.","Romans 15:13"],"03-29":["For the preaching of the cross is to them that perish foolishness; but unto us which are saved it is the power of God.","1 Corinthians 1:18"],"03-30":["But as it is written, Eye hath not seen, nor ear heard, neither have entered into the heart of man, the things which God hath prepared for them that love him.","1 Corinthians 2:9"],"03-31":["Know ye not that ye are the temple of God, and that the Spirit of God dwelleth in you?","1 Corinthians 3:16"],"04-01":["There hath no temptation taken you but such as is common to man: but God is faithful, who will not suffer you to be tempted above that ye are able; but will with the temptation also make a way to escape, that ye may be able to bear it.","1 Corinthians 10:13"],"04-02":["Charity suffereth long, and is kind; charity envieth not; charity vaunteth not itself, is not puffed up…","1 Corinthians 13:4"],"04-03":["Beareth all things, believeth all things, hopeth all things, endureth all things.","1 Corinthians 13:7"],"04-04":["And now abideth faith, hope, charity, these three; but the greatest of these is charity.","1 Corinthians 13:13"],"04-05":["O death, where is thy sting? O grave, where is thy victory?","1 Corinthians 15:55"],"04-06":["Let all your things be done with charity.","1 Corinthians 16:14"],"04-07":["While we look not at the things which are seen, but at the things which are not seen: for the things which are seen are temporal; but the things which are not seen are eternal.","2 Corinthians 4:18"],"04-08":["Therefore if any man be in Christ, he is a new creature: old things are passed away; behold, all things are become new.","2 Corinthians 5:17"],"04-09":["Every man according as he purposeth in his heart, so let him give; not grudgingly, or of necessity: for God loveth a cheerful giver.","2 Corinthians 9:7"],"04-10":["And he said unto me, My grace is sufficient for thee: for my strength is made perfect in weakness. Most gladly therefore will I rather glory in my infirmities, that the power of Christ may rest upon me.","2 Corinthians 12:9"],"04-11":["I am crucified with Christ: nevertheless I live; yet not I, but Christ liveth in me: and the life which I now live in the flesh I live by the faith of the Son of God, who loved me, and gave himself for me.","Galatians 2:20"],"04-12":["But the fruit of the Spirit is love, joy, peace, longsuffering, gentleness, goodness, faith, Meekness, temperance: against such there is no law.","Galatians 5:22-23"],"04-13":["Bear ye one another’s burdens, and so fulfil the law of Christ.","Galatians 6:2"],"04-14":["And let us not be weary in well doing: for in due season we shall reap, if we faint not.","Galatians 6:9"],"04-15":["For by grace are ye saved through faith; and that not of yourselves: it is the gift of God…","Ephesians 2:8"],"04-16":["With all lowliness and meekness, with longsuffering, forbearing one another in love…","Ephesians 4:2"],"04-17":["Be ye angry, and sin not: let not the sun go down upon your wrath…","Ephesians 4:26"],"04-18":["And be ye kind one to another, tenderhearted, forgiving one another, even as God for Christ’s sake hath forgiven you.","Ephesians 4:32"],"04-19":["For ye were sometimes darkness, but now are ye light in the Lord: walk as children of light…","Ephesians 5:8"],"04-20":["Finally, my brethren, be strong in the Lord, and in the power of his might.","Ephesians 6:10"],"04-21":["For to me to live is Christ, and to die is gain.","Philippians 1:21"],"04-22":["Let this mind be in you, which was also in Christ Jesus…","Philippians 2:5"],"04-23":["Rejoice in the Lord alway: and again I say, Rejoice.","Philippians 4:4"],"04-24":["Be careful for nothing; but in every thing by prayer and supplication with thanksgiving let your requests be made known unto God.","Philippians 4:6"],"04-25":["And the peace of God, which passeth all understanding, shall keep your hearts and minds through Christ Jesus.","Philippians 4:7"],"04-26":["Finally, brethren, whatsoever things are true, whatsoever things are honest, whatsoever things are just, whatsoever things are pure, whatsoever things are lovely, whatsoever things are of good report; if there be any virtue, and if there be any praise, think on these things.","Philippians 4:8"],"04-27":["I can do all things through Christ which strengtheneth me.","Philippians 4:13"],"04-28":["Set your affection on things above, not on things on the earth.","Colossians 3:2"],"04-29":["Forbearing one another, and forgiving one another, if any man have a quarrel against any: even as Christ forgave you, so also do ye.","Colossians 3:13"],"04-30":["And above all these things put on charity, which is the bond of perfectness.","Colossians 3:14"],"05-01":["And whatsoever ye do, do it heartily, as to the Lord, and not unto men…","Colossians 3:23"],"05-02":["Rejoice evermore. Pray without ceasing. In every thing give thanks: for this is the will of God in Christ Jesus concerning you.","1 Thessalonians 5:16-18"],"05-03":["Prove all things; hold fast that which is good.","1 Thessalonians 5:21"],"05-04":["But the Lord is faithful, who shall stablish you, and keep you from evil.","2 Thessalonians 3:3"],"05-05":["Let no man despise thy youth; but be thou an example of the believers, in word, in conversation, in charity, in spirit, in faith, in purity.","1 Timothy 4:12"],"05-06":["But godliness with contentment is great gain.","1 Timothy 6:6"],"05-07":["Fight the good fight of faith, lay hold on eternal life, whereunto thou art also called, and hast professed a good profession before many witnesses.","1 Timothy 6:12"],"05-08":["For God hath not given us the spirit of fear; but of power, and of love, and of a sound mind.","2 Timothy 1:7"],"05-09":["All scripture is given by inspiration of God, and is profitable for doctrine, for reproof, for correction, for instruction in righteousness…","2 Timothy 3:16"],"05-10":["I have fought a good fight, I have finished my course, I have kept the faith…","2 Timothy 4:7"],"05-11":["For the grace of God that bringeth salvation hath appeared to all men…","Titus 2:11"],"05-12":["Let us therefore come boldly unto the throne of grace, that we may obtain mercy, and find grace to help in time of need.","Hebrews 4:16"],"05-13":["Let us hold fast the profession of our faith without wavering; (for he is faithful that promised;)…","Hebrews 10:23"],"05-14":["Now faith is the substance of things hoped for, the evidence of things not seen.","Hebrews 11:1"],"05-15":["Wherefore seeing we also are compassed about with so great a cloud of witnesses, let us lay aside every weight, and the sin which doth so easily beset us, and let us run with patience the race that is set before us…","Hebrews 12:1"],"05-16":["Looking unto Jesus the author and finisher of our faith; who for the joy that was set before him endured the cross, despising the shame, and is set down at the right hand of the throne of God.","Hebrews 12:2"],"05-17":["Be not forgetful to entertain strangers: for thereby some have entertained angels unawares.","Hebrews 13:2"],"05-18":["Let your conversation be without covetousness; and be content with such things as ye have: for he hath said, I will never leave thee, nor forsake thee.","Hebrews 13:5"],"05-19":["Jesus Christ the same yesterday, and to day, and for ever.","Hebrews 13:8"],"05-20":["If any of you lack wisdom, let him ask of God, that giveth to all men liberally, and upbraideth not; and it shall be given him.","James 1:5"],"05-21":["Blessed is the man that endureth temptation: for when he is tried, he shall receive the crown of life, which the Lord hath promised to them that love him.","James 1:12"],"05-22":["Every good gift and every perfect gift is from above, and cometh down from the Father of lights, with whom is no variableness, neither shadow of turning.","James 1:17"],"05-23":["Wherefore, my beloved brethren, let every man be swift to hear, slow to speak, slow to wrath…","James 1:19"],"05-24":["But be ye doers of the word, and not hearers only, deceiving your own selves.","James 1:22"],"05-25":["Even so faith, if it hath not works, is dead, being alone.","James 2:17"],"05-26":["Draw nigh to God, and he will draw nigh to you. Cleanse your hands, ye sinners; and purify your hearts, ye double minded.","James 4:8"],"05-27":["Humble yourselves in the sight of the Lord, and he shall lift you up.","James 4:10"],"05-28":["Confess your faults one to another, and pray one for another, that ye may be healed. The effectual fervent prayer of a righteous man availeth much.","James 5:16"],"05-29":["But as he which hath called you is holy, so be ye holy in all manner of conversation…","1 Peter 1:15"],"05-30":["But sanctify the Lord God in your hearts: and be ready always to give an answer to every man that asketh you a reason of the hope that is in you with meekness and fear…","1 Peter 3:15"],"05-31":["And above all things have fervent charity among yourselves: for charity shall cover the multitude of sins.","1 Peter 4:8"],"06-01":["Casting all your care upon him; for he careth for you.","1 Peter 5:7"],"06-02":["Be sober, be vigilant; because your adversary the devil, as a roaring lion, walketh about, seeking whom he may devour…","1 Peter 5:8"],"06-03":["The Lord is not slack concerning his promise, as some men count slackness; but is longsuffering to us-ward, not willing that any should perish, but that all should come to repentance.","2 Peter 3:9"],"06-04":["This then is the message which we have heard of him, and declare unto you, that God is light, and in him is no darkness at all.","1 John 1:5"],"06-05":["If we confess our sins, he is faithful and just to forgive us our sins, and to cleanse us from all unrighteousness.","1 John 1:9"],"06-06":["Behold, what manner of love the Father hath bestowed upon us, that we should be called the sons of God: therefore the world knoweth us not, because it knew him not.","1 John 3:1"],"06-07":["My little children, let us not love in word, neither in tongue; but in deed and in truth.","1 John 3:18"],"06-08":["Beloved, let us love one another: for love is of God; and every one that loveth is born of God, and knoweth God.","1 John 4:7"],"06-09":["He that loveth not knoweth not God; for God is love.","1 John 4:8"],"06-10":["And we have known and believed the love that God hath to us. God is love; and he that dwelleth in love dwelleth in God, and God in him.","1 John 4:16"],"06-11":["There is no fear in love; but perfect love casteth out fear: because fear hath torment. He that feareth is not made perfect in love.","1 John 4:18"],"06-12":["We love him, because he first loved us.","1 John 4:19"],"06-13":["For whatsoever is born of God overcometh the world: and this is the victory that overcometh the world, even our faith.","1 John 5:4"],"06-14":["Behold, I stand at the door, and knock: if any man hear my voice, and open the door, I will come in to him, and will sup with him, and he with me.","Revelation 3:20"],"06-15":["And God shall wipe away all tears from their eyes; and there shall be no more death, neither sorrow, nor crying, neither shall there be any more pain: for the former things are passed away.","Revelation 21:4"],"06-16":["And he that sat upon the throne said, Behold, I make all things new. And he said unto me, Write: for these words are true and faithful.","Revelation 21:5"],"06-17":["I am Alpha and Omega, the beginning and the end, the first and the last.","Revelation 22:13"],"06-18":["In the beginning God created the heaven and the earth.","Genesis 1:1"],"06-19":["And God said, Let there be light: and there was light.","Genesis 1:3"],"06-20":["So God created man in his own image, in the image of God created he him; male and female created he them.","Genesis 1:27"],"06-21":["And God saw every thing that he had made, and, behold, it was very good. And the evening and the morning were the sixth day.","Genesis 1:31"],"06-22":["And the Lord God formed man of the dust of the ground, and breathed into his nostrils the breath of life; and man became a living soul.","Genesis 2:7"],"06-23":["And I will make of thee a great nation, and I will bless thee, and make thy name great; and thou shalt be a blessing…","Genesis 12:2"],"06-24":["And, behold, I am with thee, and will keep thee in all places whither thou goest, and will bring thee again into this land; for I will not leave thee, until I have done that which I have spoken to thee of.","Genesis 28:15"],"06-25":["And God said unto Moses, I AM THAT I AM: and he said, Thus shalt thou say unto the children of Israel, I AM hath sent me unto you.","Exodus 3:14"],"06-26":["The Lord shall fight for you, and ye shall hold your peace.","Exodus 14:14"],"06-27":["The Lord is my strength and song, and he is become my salvation: he is my God, and I will prepare him an habitation; my father’s God, and I will exalt him.","Exodus 15:2"],"06-28":["Honour thy father and thy mother: that thy days may be long upon the land which the Lord thy God giveth thee.","Exodus 20:12"],"06-29":["Thou shalt not avenge, nor bear any grudge against the children of thy people, but thou shalt love thy neighbour as thyself: I am the Lord.","Leviticus 19:18"],"06-30":["The Lord bless thee, and keep thee: The Lord make his face shine upon thee, and be gracious unto thee: The Lord lift up his countenance upon thee, and give thee peace.","Numbers 6:24-26"],"07-01":["Hear, O Israel: The Lord our God is one Lord: And thou shalt love the Lord thy God with all thine heart, and with all thy soul, and with all thy might.","Deuteronomy 6:4-5"],"07-02":["Be strong and of a good courage, fear not, nor be afraid of them: for the Lord thy God, he it is that doth go with thee; he will not fail thee, nor forsake thee.","Deuteronomy 31:6"],"07-03":["And the Lord, he it is that doth go before thee; he will be with thee, he will not fail thee, neither forsake thee: fear not, neither be dismayed.","Deuteronomy 31:8"],"07-04":["Have not I commanded thee? Be strong and of a good courage; be not afraid, neither be thou dismayed: for the Lord thy God is with thee whithersoever thou goest.","Joshua 1:9"],"07-05":["And if it seem evil unto you to serve the Lord, choose you this day whom ye will serve; whether the gods which your fathers served that were on the other side of the flood, or the gods of the Amorites, in whose land ye dwell: but as for me and my house, we will serve the Lord.","Joshua 24:15"],"07-06":["But the Lord said unto Samuel, Look not on his countenance, or on the height of his stature; because I have refused him: for the Lord seeth not as man seeth; for man looketh on the outward appearance, but the Lord looketh on the heart.","1 Samuel 16:7"],"07-07":["And he said, The Lord is my rock, and my fortress, and my deliverer…","2 Samuel 22:2"],"07-08":["For thou art my lamp, O Lord: and the Lord will lighten my darkness.","2 Samuel 22:29"],"07-09":["And after the earthquake a fire; but the Lord was not in the fire: and after the fire a still small voice.","1 Kings 19:12"],"07-10":["O give thanks unto the Lord; for he is good; for his mercy endureth for ever.","1 Chronicles 16:34"],"07-11":["If my people, which are called by my name, shall humble themselves, and pray, and seek my face, and turn from their wicked ways; then will I hear from heaven, and will forgive their sin, and will heal their land.","2 Chronicles 7:14"],"07-12":["Then he said unto them, Go your way, eat the fat, and drink the sweet, and send portions unto them for whom nothing is prepared: for this day is holy unto our Lord: neither be ye sorry; for the joy of the Lord is your strength.","Nehemiah 8:10"],"07-13":["And said, Naked came I out of my mother’s womb, and naked shall I return thither: the Lord gave, and the Lord hath taken away; blessed be the name of the Lord.","Job 1:21"],"07-14":["For I know that my redeemer liveth, and that he shall stand at the latter day upon the earth…","Job 19:25"],"07-15":["Blessed is the man that walketh not in the counsel of the ungodly, nor standeth in the way of sinners, nor sitteth in the seat of the scornful.","Psalm 1:1"],"07-16":["I will both lay me down in peace, and sleep: for thou, Lord, only makest me dwell in safety.","Psalm 4:8"],"07-17":["I have set the Lord always before me: because he is at my right hand, I shall not be moved.","Psalm 16:8"],"07-18":["Thou wilt shew me the path of life: in thy presence is fulness of joy; at thy right hand there are pleasures for evermore.","Psalm 16:11"],"07-19":["The Lord is my rock, and my fortress, and my deliverer; my God, my strength, in whom I will trust; my buckler, and the horn of my salvation, and my high tower.","Psalm 18:2"],"07-20":["The heavens declare the glory of God; and the firmament sheweth his handywork.","Psalm 19:1"],"07-21":["The Lord is my shepherd; I shall not want.","Psalm 23:1"],"07-22":["Yea, though I walk through the valley of the shadow of death, I will fear no evil: for thou art with me; thy rod and thy staff they comfort me.","Psalm 23:4"],"07-23":["Shew me thy ways, O Lord; teach me thy paths.","Psalm 25:4"],"07-24":["The Lord is my light and my salvation; whom shall I fear? the Lord is the strength of my life; of whom shall I be afraid?","Psalm 27:1"],"07-25":["Wait on the Lord: be of good courage, and he shall strengthen thine heart: wait, I say, on the Lord.","Psalm 27:14"],"07-26":["Be of good courage, and he shall strengthen your heart, all ye that hope in the Lord.","Psalm 31:24"],"07-27":["I will instruct thee and teach thee in the way which thou shalt go: I will guide thee with mine eye.","Psalm 32:8"],"07-28":["Let thy mercy, O Lord, be upon us, according as we hope in thee.","Psalm 33:22"],"07-29":["O taste and see that the Lord is good: blessed is the man that trusteth in him.","Psalm 34:8"],"07-30":["The Lord is nigh unto them that are of a broken heart; and saveth such as be of a contrite spirit.","Psalm 34:18"],"07-31":["Delight thyself also in the Lord; and he shall give thee the desires of thine heart.","Psalm 37:4"],"08-01":["Commit thy way unto the Lord; trust also in him; and he shall bring it to pass.","Psalm 37:5"],"08-02":["I waited patiently for the Lord; and he inclined unto me, and heard my cry.","Psalm 40:1"],"08-03":["As the hart panteth after the water brooks, so panteth my soul after thee, O God.","Psalm 42:1"],"08-04":["God is our refuge and strength, a very present help in trouble.","Psalm 46:1"],"08-05":["Be still, and know that I am God: I will be exalted among the heathen, I will be exalted in the earth.","Psalm 46:10"],"08-06":["Create in me a clean heart, O God; and renew a right spirit within me.","Psalm 51:10"],"08-07":["Restore unto me the joy of thy salvation; and uphold me with thy free spirit.","Psalm 51:12"],"08-08":["The sacrifices of God are a broken spirit: a broken and a contrite heart, O God, thou wilt not despise.","Psalm 51:17"],"08-09":["Cast thy burden upon the Lord, and he shall sustain thee: he shall never suffer the righteous to be moved.","Psalm 55:22"],"08-10":["What time I am afraid, I will trust in thee.","Psalm 56:3"],"08-11":["Truly my soul waiteth upon God: from him cometh my salvation.","Psalm 62:1"],"08-12":["O God, thou art my God; early will I seek thee: my soul thirsteth for thee, my flesh longeth for thee in a dry and thirsty land, where no water is…","Psalm 63:1"],"08-13":["My flesh and my heart faileth: but God is the strength of my heart, and my portion for ever.","Psalm 73:26"],"08-14":["For a day in thy courts is better than a thousand. I had rather be a doorkeeper in the house of my God, than to dwell in the tents of wickedness.","Psalm 84:10"],"08-15":["For thou, Lord, art good, and ready to forgive; and plenteous in mercy unto all them that call upon thee.","Psalm 86:5"],"08-16":["So teach us to number our days, that we may apply our hearts unto wisdom.","Psalm 90:12"],"08-17":["He that dwelleth in the secret place of the most High shall abide under the shadow of the Almighty.","Psalm 91:1"],"08-18":["For he shall give his angels charge over thee, to keep thee in all thy ways.","Psalm 91:11"],"08-19":["O come, let us worship and bow down: let us kneel before the Lord our maker.","Psalm 95:6"],"08-20":["Serve the Lord with gladness: come before his presence with singing.","Psalm 100:2"],"08-21":["Bless the Lord, O my soul, and forget not all his benefits…","Psalm 103:2"],"08-22":["The Lord is merciful and gracious, slow to anger, and plenteous in mercy.","Psalm 103:8"],"08-23":["Like as a father pitieth his children, so the Lord pitieth them that fear him.","Psalm 103:13"],"08-24":["This is the day which the Lord hath made; we will rejoice and be glad in it.","Psalm 118:24"],"08-25":["Thy word is a lamp unto my feet, and a light unto my path.","Psalm 119:105"],"08-26":["I will lift up mine eyes unto the hills, from whence cometh my help. My help cometh from the Lord, which made heaven and earth.","Psalm 121:1-2"],"08-27":["The Lord shall preserve thy going out and thy coming in from this time forth, and even for evermore.","Psalm 121:8"],"08-28":["Behold, how good and how pleasant it is for brethren to dwell together in unity!","Psalm 133:1"],"08-29":["O give thanks unto the Lord; for he is good: for his mercy endureth for ever.","Psalm 136:1"],"08-30":["I will praise thee; for I am fearfully and wonderfully made: marvellous are thy works; and that my soul knoweth right well.","Psalm 139:14"],"08-31":["Let my prayer be set forth before thee as incense; and the lifting up of my hands as the evening sacrifice.","Psalm 141:2"],"09-01":["Cause me to hear thy lovingkindness in the morning; for in thee do I trust: cause me to know the way wherein I should walk; for I lift up my soul unto thee.","Psalm 143:8"],"09-02":["The Lord is nigh unto all them that call upon him, to all that call upon him in truth.","Psalm 145:18"],"09-03":["Let every thing that hath breath praise the Lord. Praise ye the Lord.","Psalm 150:6"],"09-04":["Trust in the Lord with all thine heart; and lean not unto thine own understanding.","Proverbs 3:5"],"09-05":["In all thy ways acknowledge him, and he shall direct thy paths.","Proverbs 3:6"],"09-06":["Keep thy heart with all diligence; for out of it are the issues of life.","Proverbs 4:23"],"09-07":["I love them that love me; and those that seek me early shall find me.","Proverbs 8:17"],"09-08":["The fear of the Lord is the beginning of wisdom: and the knowledge of the holy is understanding.","Proverbs 9:10"],"09-09":["A soft answer turneth away wrath: but grievous words stir up anger.","Proverbs 15:1"],"09-10":["Commit thy works unto the Lord, and thy thoughts shall be established.","Proverbs 16:3"],"09-11":["A man’s heart deviseth his way: but the Lord directeth his steps.","Proverbs 16:9"],"09-12":["A friend loveth at all times, and a brother is born for adversity.","Proverbs 17:17"],"09-13":["The name of the Lord is a strong tower: the righteous runneth into it, and is safe.","Proverbs 18:10"],"09-14":["There are many devices in a man’s heart; nevertheless the counsel of the Lord, that shall stand.","Proverbs 19:21"],"09-15":["Train up a child in the way he should go: and when he is old, he will not depart from it.","Proverbs 22:6"],"09-16":["To every thing there is a season, and a time to every purpose under the heaven…","Ecclesiastes 3:1"],"09-17":["Two are better than one; because they have a good reward for their labour.","Ecclesiastes 4:9"],"09-18":["Let us hear the conclusion of the whole matter: Fear God, and keep his commandments: for this is the whole duty of man.","Ecclesiastes 12:13"],"09-19":["Many waters cannot quench love, neither can the floods drown it: if a man would give all the substance of his house for love, it would utterly be contemned.","Song of Songs 8:7"],"09-20":["Learn to do well; seek judgment, relieve the oppressed, judge the fatherless, plead for the widow.","Isaiah 1:17"],"09-21":["Come now, and let us reason together, saith the Lord: though your sins be as scarlet, they shall be as white as snow; though they be red like crimson, they shall be as wool.","Isaiah 1:18"],"09-22":["Thou wilt keep him in perfect peace, whose mind is stayed on thee: because he trusteth in thee.","Isaiah 26:3"],"09-23":["For thus saith the Lord God, the Holy One of Israel; In returning and rest shall ye be saved; in quietness and in confidence shall be your strength: and ye would not.","Isaiah 30:15"],"09-24":["The grass withereth, the flower fadeth: but the word of our God shall stand for ever.","Isaiah 40:8"],"09-25":["He giveth power to the faint; and to them that have no might he increaseth strength.","Isaiah 40:29"],"09-26":["But they that wait upon the Lord shall renew their strength; they shall mount up with wings as eagles; they shall run, and not be weary; and they shall walk, and not faint.","Isaiah 40:31"],"09-27":["Fear thou not; for I am with thee: be not dismayed; for I am thy God: I will strengthen thee; yea, I will help thee; yea, I will uphold thee with the right hand of my righteousness.","Isaiah 41:10"],"09-28":["But now thus saith the Lord that created thee, O Jacob, and he that formed thee, O Israel, Fear not: for I have redeemed thee, I have called thee by thy name; thou art mine.","Isaiah 43:1"],"09-29":["When thou passest through the waters, I will be with thee; and through the rivers, they shall not overflow thee: when thou walkest through the fire, thou shalt not be burned; neither shall the flame kindle upon thee.","Isaiah 43:2"],"09-30":["Behold, I will do a new thing; now it shall spring forth; shall ye not know it? I will even make a way in the wilderness, and rivers in the desert.","Isaiah 43:19"],"10-01":["Can a woman forget her sucking child, that she should not have compassion on the son of her womb? yea, they may forget, yet will I not forget thee.","Isaiah 49:15"],"10-02":["But he was wounded for our transgressions, he was bruised for our iniquities: the chastisement of our peace was upon him; and with his stripes we are healed.","Isaiah 53:5"],"10-03":["For the mountains shall depart, and the hills be removed; but my kindness shall not depart from thee, neither shall the covenant of my peace be removed, saith the Lord that hath mercy on thee.","Isaiah 54:10"],"10-04":["Seek ye the Lord while he may be found, call ye upon him while he is near…","Isaiah 55:6"],"10-05":["For my thoughts are not your thoughts, neither are your ways my ways, saith the Lord.","Isaiah 55:8"],"10-06":["And the Lord shall guide thee continually, and satisfy thy soul in drought, and make fat thy bones: and thou shalt be like a watered garden, and like a spring of water, whose waters fail not.","Isaiah 58:11"],"10-07":["Arise, shine; for thy light is come, and the glory of the Lord is risen upon thee.","Isaiah 60:1"],"10-08":["The Spirit of the Lord God is upon me; because the Lord hath anointed me to preach good tidings unto the meek; he hath sent me to bind up the brokenhearted, to proclaim liberty to the captives, and the opening of the prison to them that are bound…","Isaiah 61:1"],"10-09":["But now, O Lord, thou art our father; we are the clay, and thou our potter; and we all are the work of thy hand.","Isaiah 64:8"],"10-10":["Blessed is the man that trusteth in the Lord, and whose hope the Lord is.","Jeremiah 17:7"],"10-11":["For I know the thoughts that I think toward you, saith the Lord, thoughts of peace, and not of evil, to give you an expected end.","Jeremiah 29:11"],"10-12":["And ye shall seek me, and find me, when ye shall search for me with all your heart.","Jeremiah 29:13"],"10-13":["The Lord hath appeared of old unto me, saying, Yea, I have loved thee with an everlasting love: therefore with lovingkindness have I drawn thee.","Jeremiah 31:3"],"10-14":["Call unto me, and I will answer thee, and shew thee great and mighty things, which thou knowest not.","Jeremiah 33:3"],"10-15":["It is of the Lord’s mercies that we are not consumed, because his compassions fail not. They are new every morning: great is thy faithfulness.","Lamentations 3:22-23"],"10-16":["The Lord is good unto them that wait for him, to the soul that seeketh him.","Lamentations 3:25"],"10-17":["A new heart also will I give you, and a new spirit will I put within you: and I will take away the stony heart out of your flesh, and I will give you an heart of flesh.","Ezekiel 36:26"],"10-18":["Daniel answered and said, Blessed be the name of God for ever and ever: for wisdom and might are his…","Daniel 2:20"],"10-19":["For I desired mercy, and not sacrifice; and the knowledge of God more than burnt offerings.","Hosea 6:6"],"10-20":["Who is wise, and he shall understand these things? prudent, and he shall know them? for the ways of the Lord are right, and the just shall walk in them: but the transgressors shall fall therein.","Hosea 14:9"],"10-21":["And rend your heart, and not your garments, and turn unto the Lord your God: for he is gracious and merciful, slow to anger, and of great kindness, and repenteth him of the evil.","Joel 2:13"],"10-22":["But let judgment run down as waters, and righteousness as a mighty stream.","Amos 5:24"],"10-23":["But I will sacrifice unto thee with the voice of thanksgiving; I will pay that that I have vowed. Salvation is of the Lord.","Jonah 2:9"],"10-24":["He hath shewed thee, O man, what is good; and what doth the Lord require of thee, but to do justly, and to love mercy, and to walk humbly with thy God?","Micah 6:8"],"10-25":["Therefore I will look unto the Lord; I will wait for the God of my salvation: my God will hear me.","Micah 7:7"],"10-26":["The Lord is good, a strong hold in the day of trouble; and he knoweth them that trust in him.","Nahum 1:7"],"10-27":["Yet I will rejoice in the Lord, I will joy in the God of my salvation.","Habakkuk 3:18"],"10-28":["The Lord thy God in the midst of thee is mighty; he will save, he will rejoice over thee with joy; he will rest in his love, he will joy over thee with singing.","Zephaniah 3:17"],"10-29":["The glory of this latter house shall be greater than of the former, saith the Lord of hosts: and in this place will I give peace, saith the Lord of hosts.","Haggai 2:9"],"10-30":["Then he answered and spake unto me, saying, This is the word of the Lord unto Zerubbabel, saying, Not by might, nor by power, but by my spirit, saith the Lord of hosts.","Zechariah 4:6"],"10-31":["For I am the Lord, I change not; therefore ye sons of Jacob are not consumed.","Malachi 3:6"],"11-01":["But he answered and said, It is written, Man shall not live by bread alone, but by every word that proceedeth out of the mouth of God.","Matthew 4:4"],"11-02":["From that time Jesus began to preach, and to say, Repent: for the kingdom of heaven is at hand.","Matthew 4:17"],"11-03":["Blessed are they which are persecuted for righteousness’ sake: for theirs is the kingdom of heaven.","Matthew 5:10"],"11-04":["Ye are the salt of the earth: but if the salt have lost his savour, wherewith shall it be salted? it is thenceforth good for nothing, but to be cast out, and to be trodden under foot of men.","Matthew 5:13"],"11-05":["Be ye therefore perfect, even as your Father which is in heaven is perfect.","Matthew 5:48"],"11-06":["After this manner therefore pray ye: Our Father which art in heaven, Hallowed be thy name. Thy kingdom come. Thy will be done in earth, as it is in heaven.","Matthew 6:9-10"],"11-07":["For if ye forgive men their trespasses, your heavenly Father will also forgive you…","Matthew 6:14"],"11-08":["Judge not, that ye be not judged.","Matthew 7:1"],"11-09":["But go ye and learn what that meaneth, I will have mercy, and not sacrifice: for I am not come to call the righteous, but sinners to repentance.","Matthew 9:13"],"11-10":["Heal the sick, cleanse the lepers, raise the dead, cast out devils: freely ye have received, freely give.","Matthew 10:8"],"11-11":["But the very hairs of your head are all numbered. Fear ye not therefore, ye are of more value than many sparrows.","Matthew 10:30-31"],"11-12":["But straightway Jesus spake unto them, saying, Be of good cheer; it is I; be not afraid.","Matthew 14:27"],"11-13":["Then said Jesus unto his disciples, If any man will come after me, let him deny himself, and take up his cross, and follow me.","Matthew 16:24"],"11-14":["For what is a man profited, if he shall gain the whole world, and lose his own soul? or what shall a man give in exchange for his soul?","Matthew 16:26"],"11-15":["And Jesus said unto them, Because of your unbelief: for verily I say unto you, If ye have faith as a grain of mustard seed, ye shall say unto this mountain, Remove hence to yonder place; and it shall remove; and nothing shall be impossible unto you.","Matthew 17:20"],"11-16":["But Jesus said, Suffer little children, and forbid them not, to come unto me: for of such is the kingdom of heaven.","Matthew 19:14"],"11-17":["But Jesus beheld them, and said unto them, With men this is impossible; but with God all things are possible.","Matthew 19:26"],"11-18":["Even as the Son of man came not to be ministered unto, but to minister, and to give his life a ransom for many.","Matthew 20:28"],"11-19":["Heaven and earth shall pass away, but my words shall not pass away.","Matthew 24:35"],"11-20":["Watch and pray, that ye enter not into temptation: the spirit indeed is willing, but the flesh is weak.","Matthew 26:41"],"11-21":["For what shall it profit a man, if he shall gain the whole world, and lose his own soul?","Mark 8:36"],"11-22":["For even the Son of man came not to be ministered unto, but to minister, and to give his life a ransom for many.","Mark 10:45"],"11-23":["Watch ye and pray, lest ye enter into temptation. The spirit truly is ready, but the flesh is weak.","Mark 14:38"],"11-24":["And Mary said, Behold the handmaid of the Lord; be it unto me according to thy word. And the angel departed from her.","Luke 1:38"],"11-25":["I came not to call the righteous, but sinners to repentance.","Luke 5:32"],"11-26":["And he said to them all, If any man will come after me, let him deny himself, and take up his cross daily, and follow me.","Luke 9:23"],"11-27":["And he answering said, Thou shalt love the Lord thy God with all thy heart, and with all thy soul, and with all thy strength, and with all thy mind; and thy neighbour as thyself.","Luke 10:27"],"11-28":["And he said unto them, Take heed, and beware of covetousness: for a man’s life consisteth not in the abundance of the things which he possesseth.","Luke 12:15"],"11-29":["He that is faithful in that which is least is faithful also in much: and he that is unjust in the least is unjust also in much.","Luke 16:10"],"11-30":["Neither shall they say, Lo here! or, lo there! for, behold, the kingdom of God is within you.","Luke 17:21"],"12-01":["For the Son of man is come to seek and to save that which was lost.","Luke 19:10"],"12-02":["Saying, Father, if thou be willing, remove this cup from me: nevertheless not my will, but thine, be done.","Luke 22:42"],"12-03":["In him was life; and the life was the light of men.","John 1:4"],"12-04":["But as many as received him, to them gave he power to become the sons of God, even to them that believe on his name…","John 1:12"],"12-05":["The next day John seeth Jesus coming unto him, and saith, Behold the Lamb of God, which taketh away the sin of the world.","John 1:29"],"12-06":["All that the Father giveth me shall come to me; and him that cometh to me I will in no wise cast out.","John 6:37"],"12-07":["Then Simon Peter answered him, Lord, to whom shall we go? thou hast the words of eternal life.","John 6:68"],"12-08":["In the last day, that great day of the feast, Jesus stood and cried, saying, If any man thirst, let him come unto me, and drink.","John 7:37"],"12-09":["The thief cometh not, but for to steal, and to kill, and to destroy: I am come that they might have life, and that they might have it more abundantly.","John 10:10"],"12-10":["I am come a light into the world, that whosoever believeth on me should not abide in darkness.","John 12:46"],"12-11":["Let not your heart be troubled: ye believe in God, believe also in me.","John 14:1"],"12-12":["In my Father’s house are many mansions: if it were not so, I would have told you. I go to prepare a place for you.","John 14:2"],"12-13":["If ye love me, keep my commandments.","John 14:15"],"12-14":["Jesus answered and said unto him, If a man love me, he will keep my words: and my Father will love him, and we will come unto him, and make our abode with him.","John 14:23"],"12-15":["Abide in me, and I in you. As the branch cannot bear fruit of itself, except it abide in the vine; no more can ye, except ye abide in me.","John 15:4"],"12-16":["If ye abide in me, and my words abide in you, ye shall ask what ye will, and it shall be done unto you.","John 15:7"],"12-17":["These things have I spoken unto you, that my joy might remain in you, and that your joy might be full.","John 15:11"],"12-18":["Hitherto have ye asked nothing in my name: ask, and ye shall receive, that your joy may be full.","John 16:24"],"12-19":["Therefore the Lord himself shall give you a sign; Behold, a virgin shall conceive, and bear a son, and shall call his name Immanuel.","Isaiah 7:14"],"12-20":["But thou, Beth–lehem Ephratah, though thou be little among the thousands of Judah, yet out of thee shall he come forth unto me that is to be ruler in Israel; whose goings forth have been from of old, from everlasting.","Micah 5:2"],"12-21":["Through the tender mercy of our God; whereby the dayspring from on high hath visited us, To give light to them that sit in darkness and in the shadow of death, to guide our feet into the way of peace.","Luke 1:78-79"],"12-22":["And she shall bring forth a son, and thou shalt call his name JESUS: for he shall save his people from their sins.","Matthew 1:21"],"12-23":["Behold, a virgin shall be with child, and shall bring forth a son, and they shall call his name Emmanuel, which being interpreted is, God with us.","Matthew 1:23"],"12-24":["And the angel said unto them, Fear not: for, behold, I bring you good tidings of great joy, which shall be to all people. For unto you is born this day in the city of David a Saviour, which is Christ the Lord.","Luke 2:10-11"],"12-25":["And when they were come into the house, they saw the young child with Mary his mother, and fell down, and worshipped him: and when they had opened their treasures, they presented unto him gifts; gold, and frankincense, and myrrh.","Matthew 2:11"],"12-26":["But when the fulness of the time was come, God sent forth his Son, made of a woman, made under the law, To redeem them that were under the law, that we might receive the adoption of sons.","Galatians 4:4-5"],"12-27":["And without controversy great is the mystery of godliness: God was manifest in the flesh, justified in the Spirit, seen of angels, preached unto the Gentiles, believed on in the world, received up into glory.","1 Timothy 3:16"],"12-28":["Not by works of righteousness which we have done, but according to his mercy he saved us, by the washing of regeneration, and renewing of the Holy Ghost…","Titus 3:5"],"12-29":["God, who at sundry times and in divers manners spake in time past unto the fathers by the prophets, Hath in these last days spoken unto us by his Son, whom he hath appointed heir of all things, by whom also he made the worlds…","Hebrews 1:1-2"],"12-30":["And of his fulness have all we received, and grace for grace.","John 1:16"],"12-31":["Before the mountains were brought forth, or ever thou hadst formed the earth and the world, even from everlasting to everlasting, thou art God.","Psalm 90:2"]};
